{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MAX_N = 510;\nusing PII = pair<int, int>;\n#define F first\n#define S second\n\nint n, m, MOD;\nint C[MAX_N][MAX_N];\nPII dp[MAX_N][MAX_N];\n\ninline int mod_add(int a, int b) {\n    a += b;\n    if (a >= MOD) a -= MOD;\n    return a;\n}\n\nPII operator+(const PII& x, const PII& y) {\n    return {mod_add(x.F, y.F), mod_add(x.S, y.S)};\n}\n\nPII operator*(const PII& x, const PII& y) {\n    long long f = (1LL * x.F * y.F) % MOD;\n    long long s = (1LL * x.F * y.S + 1LL * x.S * y.F) % MOD;\n    return {(int)f, (int)s};\n}\n\nint sum_range(int l, int r) {\n    return (l + r) * (r - l + 1) / 2;\n}\n\nint main() {\n#ifdef LOCAL\n    freopen(\"a.in\", \"r\", stdin);\n    freopen(\"a.out\", \"w\", stdout);\n#endif\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    cin >> n >> m >> MOD;\n    \n    // Precompute binomial coefficients\n    for (int i = 0; i < MAX_N; ++i) {\n        C[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j) {\n            C[i][j] = mod_add(C[i-1][j], C[i-1][j-1]);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // DP initialization and computation\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n        dp[i][0] = {1, 0};\n        for (int j = 1; j <= min(i, m); ++j) {\n            if (i != j) {\n                for (int k = 1; k <= i; ++k) {\n                    dp[i][j] = dp[i][j] + dp[k-1][k-1] * dp[i-k][j-k+1] * PII{C[j][k-1], 0};\n                }\n            } else {\n                for (int k = 1; k <= i; ++k) {\n                    int val = (i + 1) * (k * k - sum_range(1, k) + sum_range(k+1, i) - k * (i - k));\n                    dp[i][j] = dp[i][j] + dp[k-1][k-1] * dp[i-k][i-k] * PII{C[i-1][k-1], 0} * PII{val % MOD, 0};\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << dp[n][m].S << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MAX_N = 510;\n    static int n, m, MOD;\n    static int[][] C = new int[MAX_N][MAX_N];\n    static Pair[][] dp = new Pair[MAX_N][MAX_N];\n\n    static class Pair {\n        int F;\n        int S;\n\n        Pair(int f, int s) {\n            F = f;\n            S = s;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static int mod_add(int a, int b) {\n        a += b;\n        if (a >= MOD) a -= MOD;\n        return a;\n    }\n\n    static Pair add(Pair x, Pair y) {\n        return new Pair(mod_add(x.F, y.F), mod_add(x.S, y.S));\n    }\n\n    static Pair multiply(Pair x, Pair y) {\n        long f = (1L * x.F * y.F) % MOD;\n        long s = (1L * x.F * y.S + 1L * x.S * y.F) % MOD;\n        return new Pair((int) f, (int) s);\n    }\n\n    static int sum_range(int l, int r) {\n        return (l + r) * (r - l + 1) / 2;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        n = sc.nextInt();\n        m = sc.nextInt();\n        MOD = sc.nextInt();\n\n        // Precompute binomial coefficients\n        for (int i = 0; i < MAX_N; ++i) {\n            C[i][0] = 1;\n            for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j) {\n                C[i][j] = mod_add(C[i-1][j], C[i-1][j-1]);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // DP initialization and computation\n        for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n            dp[i][0] = new Pair(1, 0);\n            for (int j = 1; j <= Math.min(i, m); ++j) {\n                dp[i][j] = new Pair(0, 0);\n                if (i != j) {\n                    for (int k = 1; k <= i; ++k) {\n                        Pair term1 = dp[k-1][k-1];\n                        Pair term2 = dp[i-k][j-k+1];\n                        Pair term3 = new Pair(C[j][k-1], 0);\n                        Pair product = multiply(term1, term2);\n                        product = multiply(product, term3);\n                        dp[i][j] = add(dp[i][j], product);\n                    }\n                } else {\n                    for (int k = 1; k <= i; ++k) {\n                        int val = (i + 1) * (k * k - sum_range(1, k) + sum_range(k+1, i) - k * (i - k));\n                        Pair term1 = dp[k-1][k-1];\n                        Pair term2 = dp[i-k][i-k];\n                        Pair term3 = new Pair(C[i-1][k-1], 0);\n                        Pair term4 = new Pair(val % MOD, 0);\n                        Pair product = multiply(term1, term2);\n                        product = multiply(product, term3);\n                        product = multiply(product, term4);\n                        dp[i][j] = add(dp[i][j], product);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(dp[n][m].S);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012373158824630082, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.002033072989434004, -2.3245540432981215e-05, -0.1269887387752533, -0.43808168172836304, -8.761498611420393e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -3.576214658096433e-05, -0.02630125917494297, -0.0001588933